 Material colour, tint and shadows now live in material-system.css, with legacy paint/token declarations removed from seven style files. Content remains solid, ambient lighting is an independent noninteractive element and controls/transients have explicit layer roles. Light-theme primary-action text must retain accentink rather than inherit generic glass-control ink; a stale high-specificity rule was removed. Section transitions are a single brief, reduced-motion-aware content animation, not a cascade. Chromium desktop and a true narrow iframe rendering of the main app checked both themes, menus, charts, journal and the unsaved entry sheet. No hardware or timing benchmark is claimed.
+
+## L46 — Dock correction after box-like final tab
+The L45 horizontal lens used button width+12, left−6 and radius .34 of its short side, yielding a 2 px right gap in the 390 px diagnostic scene. L46 uses button centres, a capsule profile and a presentation boundary that includes directional deformation; the resting gap is 8 px and the minimum silhouette inset is 6 px. The substrate is masked out beneath the moving lens, retaining a small overlap at its rim. Both masks and position use the same presentation values.
+
+A concrete optical bug was established through computed CSS: L45's navigation rule overrode the generic SVG selector, leaving blur(1px) even when the data attribute said svg. The L46 horizontal selector applies its actual URL filter. Chromium contrasting-line screenshots show a changed line path; forced fallback reports frosted/blur(.6px). This does not establish Safari, GPU or native material parity. No frame/layout benchmark or continuous touch recording was made. Four repeated taps committed once, two directional desktop drags completed and narrow main-app layout/scroll/keyboard checks succeeded. The detailed evidence and untested gesture paths are in RELEASE_L46.md.
